Fix security hooks failing open on Linux/macOS; pin ruff

CI caught two stacked bugs that made every git hook silently inert on Linux
and macOS while Windows reported green. Neither emitted a warning.

  exec bit  hooks were committed 100644. Git refuses to run a non-executable
            hook and then CONTINUES, so the commit succeeds unscanned.
  CRLF      hooks were committed with CRLF, so the shebang resolved to
            '#!/bin/sh\r' -> 'bad interpreter'. Git skips the hook. Silently.

A control that fails OPEN and QUIETLY on the two platforms most likely to run
CI is worse than no control, because it manufactures false confidence. The CI
job that commits a synthetic secret is what surfaced this; without it the gap
would have shipped invisibly.

.gitattributes  root-cause fix: pins LF for .githooks/*, sources and configs;
                marks binaries. Whole repo renormalised.
hook modes      now 100755 in the git index (the filesystem bit does not
                survive a clone; the index mode is what others receive).
ruff            pinned ==0.16.3. 'ruff>=0.6' resolved to a newer release in
                CI than locally and failed on rules that did not exist when
                the code was written - dependency drift, inside an hour of
                writing a README section warning about dependency drift.

tests/test_hooks_installable.py  10 tests pinning the invariants: index mode,
                LF endings, valid shebang, .gitattributes coverage, no CRLF in
                any tracked .py, ruff pinned exactly, setup script exits 0.
                A correct scanner that never executes is worth nothing.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
